mpty; it never exercises the actual AuthSettings construction or container boot that failed. A green compose-grep passes even if the injected value is malformed such that AuthSettings still raises ValidationError (the real observed failure was 'endpoint never comes up' / crash-loop), so the test proves config presence but not that the crash-loop is resolved.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0671792f304d08ca","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"RED-first oracle / AC line 1 (compose-assertion test)","norm_id":"ne8544dd9e8169efb","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the default URL were later edited to a value AuthSettings rejects (e.g. non-URL), the compose-grep test stays green while the mcp container resumes crash-looping on deploy — the exact failure the plan set out to prevent."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Supplement the compose-grep with a test that feeds the compose default issuer URL into AuthSettings(issuer_url=..., ...) and asserts it constructs without ValidationError, or a lightweight mcp boot/health assertion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealin